{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5","id":1473917,"title":"Help me understand the Path of Night and it's role in the Sabbat (pre v5)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-03T12:38:19-08:00","id":1473917,"title":"Help me understand the Path of Night and it's role in the Sabbat (pre v5)","content":"The thing thing has bugged me for almost 20 years. How the hell does a Path of Night adherent function within the Sabbat? It's lvl 2 sin is &quot;Accepting the superiority of another&quot;. How the hell does anyone except the Regent themselves not sin against this every single time they meet a Bishop, Arch Bishop, Cardinal etc.? I mean even having a Ductus would be a sin against this path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T12:56:27-08:00","id":1473919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5#post1473917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing thing has bugged me for almost 20 years. How the hell does a Path of Night adherent function within the Sabbat? It's lvl 2 sin is &quot;Accepting the superiority of another&quot;. How the hell does anyone except the Regent themselves not sin against this every single time they meet a Bishop, Arch Bishop, Cardinal etc.? I mean even having a Ductus would be a sin against this path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's one of those things that lies in the interpretation rather than the literalness. Basically, the Path of Night states that you do not accept the superiority of any other vampire but that just means you have to plot against them and grow stronger to eventually overthrow them.<br /> <br /> It's pretty basic Sith ideology.<br /> <br /> You may be my boss today but I do not accept this. I will not be your slave and someday, you will obey ME.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T13:37:12-08:00","id":1473924,"title":"","content":"The purpose? Other than Edgelordism that can compete with the other Paths?<br /> <br /> To me its just the 'other' path of Power and Inner Voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T14:03:38-08:00","id":1473928,"title":"","content":"The Path of Night is essentially acting as a Devil would, in service of God. <br /> <br /> It is very easy to be a Saint in Paradise, but are Saints in Paradise worthy of anything? The Path of Night argues that untested virtues are not virtues, but meaningless words. Thus, they test, corrupt, and destroy humans to either prove they never deserved to be called virtuous, or prove they did in fact deserve the title. <br /> <br /> You will notice this is similar to the Embrace methods of Clan Lasombra, who created this Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T14:23:42-08:00","id":1473931,"title":"","content":"You basically fulfil the role of lucifer in the old testament as castigator of humanity rather than its tyrant. Ideas of superiority are absurd because all vampires are scum, including you.<br /> <br /> Servants of evil are servants, not masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-03-2022, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T15:09:23-08:00","id":1473935,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is the proper role of leadership and the definition of &quot;superiority&quot; to differing peoples.<br /> <br /> If you see the Sabbat episcopate as a top down organization where lower ranking people must obey their superiors, it causes problems for characters on the Path of Night. But if you believe the Sabbat is a sect with two equal principles - loyalty and freedom, it isn't an obstacle. The Loyalist faction believes in &quot;loyalty to the Sabbat through disloyalty to leaders.&quot; That fits in quite well with the Path of Night, so we should assume the Path of Night is probably one of the bulwarks of the Loyalist faction.<br /> <br /> Even a Ductus isn't necessarily an issue if you think the leader is merely a first among equals, or someone who helps settles disputes between equals so a group can accomplish something, versus a military style leader whose orders are absolute. To a pack following the Path of Night, a Ductus might simply be the designated person who speaks for the group when dealing with outsiders, not someone who tells the others what to do.<br /> <br /> None of this presents a problem with the way the Sabbat was originally portrayed which was a sect heavily divided. It only becomes an issue due to metaplot in Revised and V5 which essentially says the entire Sabbat is now like the Black Hand, which is a military organization with a strict hierarchy of obedience. This is one reason I ignore metaplot, stopped buying Revised materials, and don't support V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T22:32:20-08:00","id":1473952,"title":"","content":"Agreed with Black Fox.<br /> <br /> The inherent nature of the Sabbat - a decentralized confederation of Cainite packs brought together by mutual, communal blood bonds and for united protection against the Antedeluvians.<br /> <br /> While hierarchies exist within the larger sect (for the Sabbat is, if nothing else, a mass of hypocrisies and contradictions), a Path of Night adherent doesn't need to respect anyone in a position of authority.<br /> <br /> This is also why, even when crusades are nominally run by one Cainite Elder or another, they coach their marching orders in the form of requests, suggestions, challenges, or opportunities. Because savvy Cainites know that many Sabbat packs or individuals will not respond well to being ordered around. This is just Sabbat in general, not just Path of Night licks. Rebels and contrarians all, Cainites on crusade must by tricked, goaded, or convinced to do anything. This is both a strength and a weakness of the sect, and why every crusade involves throwing as many Cainites at a problem to see what sticks.<br /> <br /> The Path of Night simply codifies this penchant for militant &quot;you can't tell me what to do&quot; attitude into an ethical law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T03:25:02-08:00","id":1473958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473935#post1473935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to consider is the proper role of leadership and the definition of &amp;quot;superiority&amp;quot; to differing peoples.<br /> <br /> If you see the Sabbat episcopate as a top down organization where lower ranking people must obey their superiors, it causes problems for characters on the Path of Night. But if you believe the Sabbat is a sect with two equal principles - loyalty and freedom, it isn't an obstacle. The Loyalist faction believes in &amp;quot;loyalty to the Sabbat through disloyalty to leaders.&amp;quot; That fits in quite well with the Path of Night, so we should assume the Path of Night is probably one of the bulwarks of the Loyalist faction.<br /> <br /> Even a Ductus isn't necessarily an issue if you think the leader is merely a first among equals, or someone who helps settles disputes between equals so a group can accomplish something, versus a military style leader whose orders are absolute. To a pack following the Path of Night, a Ductus might simply be the designated person who speaks for the group when dealing with outsiders, not someone who tells the others what to do.<br /> <br /> None of this presents a problem with the way the Sabbat was originally portrayed which was a sect heavily divided. It only becomes an issue due to metaplot in Revised and V5 which essentially says the entire Sabbat is now like the Black Hand, which is a military organization with a strict hierarchy of obedience. This is one reason I ignore metaplot, stopped buying Revised materials, and don't support V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is by itself very curious: Path of Night should be quite important in Lasombra identity, and the Loyalist faction is an odd choice for the Sabbat's upper class. This would put Path of Night adherents as the literal &quot;black sheep&quot; of the Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T04:31:47-08:00","id":1473963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473935#post1473935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this presents a problem with the way the Sabbat was originally portrayed which was a sect heavily divided. It only becomes an issue due to metaplot in Revised and V5 which essentially says the entire Sabbat is now like the Black Hand, which is a military organization with a strict hierarchy of obedience. This is one reason I ignore metaplot, stopped buying Revised materials, and don't support V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hierarchy of the Sabbat has fallen apart in V5. Packs only follow leaders who they think are worth following.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T10:34:37-08:00","id":1473982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473958#post1473958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is by itself very curious: Path of Night should be quite important in Lasombra identity, and the Loyalist faction is an odd choice for the Sabbat's upper class. This would put Path of Night adherents as the literal &quot;black sheep&quot; of the Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or its an indication something went really wrong with how the Lasombra were presented.<br /> <br /> One of the odd things we're expected to believe is that the pre-Sabbat Lasombra and post-Sabbat Lasombra are essentially the same. There seems to be very little change in clan culture despite the Lasombra of the Anarch Revolt essentially destroying almost any member of their clan who opposed the Anarchs. Indeed, we're even told some of the Lasombra elders from the Dark Ages became Sabbat. Does that make much sense? Shouldn't we see a big cultural difference between the Sabbat Lasombra and the Lasombra anti-tribu, even if certain things like ambition and a love of intrigue are held in common? Shouldn't there have been a purge of the most tyrannical aspects of pre-Sabbat Lasombra culture as the victorious anarchs tore down hated clan traditions and instritutions? We should have seen just as much vandalism and desecration of certain Lasombra culture in the same way the French Revolutionaries did to the Ancien Regime, or the Bolsheviks did to the Tsarist and aristocratic heritage, or the Maoists did to traditional Confucian culture. The Sabbat Lasombra should be recognizably distinct from the Lasombra antitribu in some fashion, and I don't think this was ever well presented.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with seeing many Lasombra of the time of the Anarch Revolt becoming hypocrites and power hungry, betraying their old ideals for power. I also don't have a problem for some opportunistic Lasombra who heed the old ways having joined the sect. Or that as time passed on the fires of youth faded, that some aspects of the old Lasombra culture came back. But there should also be a large number of Lasombra who continue to have the ideals of the original Lasombra anarchs who supposedly fought for freedom from the elders. And this last group of Lasombra has always been neglected in the game.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to figure out a way on how to combine the original ideals of the Anarch Revolt and the core Lasombra identity of them being ambitious and masters of intrigue, you could do a lot worse than the Path of Night.<br /> <br /> I think one issue is that the Path of Night was not one of the original Paths in the first Players Guide to Sabbat. So there obviously could not be any attempt to explain the clan using that Path. Instead, it was probably felt that all Sabbat Lasombra would adhere to a path like Power and the Inner Voice, Honorable Accord, or other more obvious leadership Path. I think the Path of Night first appears in the Revised VtM corebook where it's presented as a Path almost exclusively by very young Lasombra, who are scorned by the other Lasombra. (So your black sheep comment is on the mark).<br /> <br /> And like many concepts of the game, once its out there, it is often developed further by people who see potential in something, but don't adhere closely to details. So we can get to the point where we think the Path of Night is iconic to the Lasombra until it occurs to us this undermines other aspects of the clan like the OP mentioned. So if you want to say both aspects are true, it may be better to state that the Path of Night is something <i>distinctive</i> to the Lasombra (in the sense it reveals something unique about the clan), but isn't <i>iconic</i> (in the sense that it defines the clan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T14:03:46-08:00","id":1473995,"title":"","content":"If we're getting into the nitty gritty of the Path of Night, it's also important to note that the Sabbat Path of Night is completely new and would come off the &quot;Hail Satan&quot; version of Christianity to the original Road of Night followers. The Modern Path of Night is a corruption of everything the original Road of Night stood for, which was punishing the guilty and basically being Medieval Batman.<br /> <br /> So the Modern Path of Night has no genuine &quot;historical&quot; importance to the Lasombra because it had to have been made specifically for the Sabbat Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Road_of_Night\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Road_of_Night</a><br /> <br /> <u>Rating Moral Guideline</u><br /> <br /> 10 Spending too much time in the affairs of Cainites.<br /> 9 Feeling remorse for your actions.<br /> 8 Killing any mortal without taking confession first.<br /> 7 Attempting to save a Cainite.<br /> 6 Accepting the superiority of any Cainite other than those on the Road of Night or other members of your clan.<br /> 5 Killing a sinner for any reason other than self-defense.<br /> 4 Trying to save a sinner by means that do not involve pain and suffering.<br /> 3 Allowing the corruption of mortals.<br /> 2 Embracing a sinner who is still capable of remorse and redemption.<br /> 1 Causing or bringing about the corruption of a mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-04-2022, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T14:31:23-08:00","id":1473997,"title":"","content":"Thanks Black Fox and the rest, it makes a lot more sense to look at the Sabbat as a loose confederation rather than a monolith with a strict hierarchy. Granted I was introduced to Vampire with Revised and the Sabbat via the Guide to the Sabbat and Core books of that edition so i might have seen it a bit from a weird standpoint.<br /> <br /> But I still don't really comprehend the concept of &quot;First among equals&quot;. Sure the Bishop doesn't order a pack to do something, he lets them know what he wishes and either presents it as a challenge, or an opportunity. But he still expects Cainites to recognize his status and respect him due to meritocratic structure of the Sabbat. If a lick on the Path of Night blatantly ignores him or disrespects him he will most likely either Frenzy or work towards getting that lick removed from his domain.<br /> <br /> And even if the adherent of the Path of Night doesn't outright scream &quot;you're not my dad&quot; to the Bishop he will still clean his room because &quot;dad&quot; told him to. Which to me would constitute as a violation against the lvl 2 sin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T15:32:12-08:00","id":1474005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473997#post1473997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Black Fox and the rest, it makes a lot more sense to look at the Sabbat as a loose confederation rather than a monolith with a strict hierarchy. Granted I was introduced to Vampire with Revised and the Sabbat via the Guide to the Sabbat and Core books of that edition so i might have seen it a bit from a weird standpoint.<br /> <br /> But I still don't really comprehend the concept of &quot;First among equals&quot;. Sure the Bishop doesn't order a pack to do something, he lets them know what he wishes and either presents it as a challenge, or an opportunity. But he still expects Cainites to recognize his status and respect him due to meritocratic structure of the Sabbat. If a lick on the Path of Night blatantly ignores him or disrespects him he will most likely either Frenzy or work towards getting that lick removed from his domain.<br /> <br /> And even if the adherent of the Path of Night doesn't outright scream &quot;you're not my dad&quot; to the Bishop he will still clean his room because &quot;dad&quot; told him to. Which to me would constitute as a violation against the lvl 2 sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>My suggestion then is to house rule it otherwise if it doesn't work for you. The Golden Rule and all that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T18:36:27-08:00","id":1474018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473997#post1473997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still don't really comprehend the concept of &quot;First among equals&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;First among equals&quot; is simply a phrase that indicates that while one person may have more prestige, or higher skill, or whatever, that fundamentally that person is still just an equal member of the group without any more authority or ranking than the other members. They're in a group of friends or peers, there's not hierarchy among them. Someone might choose to follow or defer to such a person, but the person isn't obeyed as if he is a superior.<br /> <br /> Such a status might be an accurate description if we're talking about the most charismatic and athletic guy in a group of friends. Or it might be a polite fiction to hide real authority like in the case when Augustus Caesar was supposedly simply the &quot;First Citizen&quot; of Rome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473997#post1473997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure the Bishop doesn't order a pack to do something, he lets them know what he wishes and either presents it as a challenge, or an opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a pack might just nod their heads and do their own thing, or just laugh in the guy's face. These are also options available to them. Whether they are the smart options or credible actions may depend on a lot of circumstances. Depending on the Sabbat domain, the power of the Bishop, the packs involved, etc., a Bishop's &quot;request&quot; might be a veiled order, letting others know there is an opportunity to kiss his ass and earn his favor, just a request for help from someone he thinks is an ally, or a pathetic beg from a weak and impotent man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473997#post1473997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he still expects Cainites to recognize his status and respect him due to meritocratic structure of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am dying laughing at the supposed &quot;meritocratic&quot; structure of the Sabbat.<br /> Certainly someone on the Path of Night (or anyone else) can acknowledge someone's status as a Bishop and be polite to him. But that does not mean the person must recognize the Bishop's <i>authority</i> over him. This is the entire dispute by the Loyalist faction of the Sabbat. What does a sect based on total freedom owe to its nominal leaders? We know what the Status Quo and Ultraconservatives factions want it to be - obedience to the Sabbat hierarchy as governed by the revised Code of Milan. We also know what the Moderates and Loyalists believe - the sect needs to lean towards more freedom.<br /> <br /> To a Loyalist or even a Moderate, &quot;respect&quot; may simply mean &quot;I will listen to your plan and consider its merits. But it is up to me if I decide to join it. I am willing to perform the Vaulderie with you to show I do not consider you an enemy, but that will bind you to me as much as it binds me to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Bishop might consider that insufficient. But that's politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473997#post1473997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a lick on the Path of Night blatantly ignores him or disrespects him he will most likely either Frenzy or work towards getting that lick removed from his domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but the opposite also holds. I think you are assuming that the Bishop is in a superior position of power to the other Sabbat. That may or may not be true.<br /> <br /> In certain Sabbat domains, the Ultraconservatives might dominate and run a very strict domain, and any signs of disobedience will be met with terrible force. But that is not true in all domains. If you're a member of a Nomad pack that spends most of their time travelling and rarely spending any time at any domain, it might be completely irrelevant what any Bishop wants. He has no means of truly enforcing his rule over you. You just leave when it becomes inconvenient. Or maybe the Bishop is new or weak, and the follower of the Path of Night could easily slay him in monomacy. Or your pack/coven is so experienced, old, large, or whatever that you have in effect more power and influence in the domain than the Bishop. Or perhaps the entire Sabbat domain is a stronghold of the Loyalist faction, and the Bishop is one of the Brujah anti-tribu who shares the same conception of leadership that the follower of the Path of Night does.<br /> <br /> Lots of scenarios are possible. It's not that what you said is wrong, it is just an incomplete analysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473997#post1473997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if the adherent of the Path of Night doesn't outright scream &quot;you're not my dad&quot; to the Bishop he will still clean his room because &quot;dad&quot; told him to. Which to me would constitute as a violation against the lvl 2 sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I explained, not necessarily. Why should a Sabbat bishop necessarily command greater obedience than does a Prince of the Camarilla? In vampire society, you can only command to the extent that you can convince or compel someone. In some domains, a Bishop's orders may be law because of the Bishop's power, his allies, trusted enforcers among the Paladins, or because of the backing of other forces like the Sabbat Inquisition or Black Hand. To defy them means death. In other domains, the Bishop might lack the power of other Sabbat in the domain, have few allies, or is being undermined by others. To defy them is normal, provided you can justify it to the other local Sabbat as being loyal to the principles of the Sect.<br /> <br /> A Bishop who doesn't have the personal power, prestige, allies, or political skill who attempts to enforce his will beyond his capabilities will suffer drawbacks. At worse, he gets killed - in secret or through monomacy. Or he might find his prestige collapsing when he's not obeyed, and then when word gets out to the other Bishops that he can't enforce his will, he loses even the respect of his peers. Or maybe the most powerful or charismatic packs simply leave his domain and go elsewhere, causing him to lose tools he might have otherwise used to shore up his power, and now his domain is weak and might fall to archons or hunters.<br /> <br /> What this means for followers of the Path of Night is that they need to choose where they live carefully. It needs to be conducive to how they act. The relative power of the Bishops need to be in their favor. Don't go to Mexico City where the Regent lives and the Ultraconservatives are in force. But there may be other domains where the Loyalists are much stronger and the authority of the Bishops is less. Or they can go on the road as a Nomad pack and mostly ignore the Bishops entirely. Don't visit that domain until you hear the Bishop has turned the Panders against him, and a founded coven there is calling in friends from elsewhere to help them put the Bishop in his place.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat hierarchy is strong in certain places and weak in others. It's ruled in some places by hardass tyrants, and others by charismatic Loyalists.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it's how the ST builds the world and whether he allows there to be places where that attitude can be done. In 2e Sabbat, there were lots of places where this could be done. But in Revised, this aspect of the sect was ignored because it got in the way of the Crusade storyline metaplot that Justin Achilli wanted to tell. In 2e, the existing power relationship that favored the Ultraconservatives was a result of the Panders siding with them in the Third Sabbat Civil War. But their rule is not absolute, and any number of changes could tilt favor back towards the Loyalists. Depending on how the ST wants to balance things and portray the setting, a lot is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-12-2022, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T01:51:43-08:00","id":1474033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1473982#post1473982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or its an indication something went really wrong with how the Lasombra were presented.<br /> <br /> One of the odd things we're expected to believe is that the pre-Sabbat Lasombra and post-Sabbat Lasombra are essentially the same. There seems to be very little change in clan culture despite the Lasombra of the Anarch Revolt essentially destroying almost any member of their clan who opposed the Anarchs. Indeed, we're even told some of the Lasombra elders from the Dark Ages became Sabbat. Does that make much sense? Shouldn't we see a big cultural difference between the Sabbat Lasombra and the Lasombra anti-tribu, even if certain things like ambition and a love of intrigue are held in common? Shouldn't there have been a purge of the most tyrannical aspects of pre-Sabbat Lasombra culture as the victorious anarchs tore down hated clan traditions and instritutions? We should have seen just as much vandalism and desecration of certain Lasombra culture in the same way the French Revolutionaries did to the Ancien Regime, or the Bolsheviks did to the Tsarist and aristocratic heritage, or the Maoists did to traditional Confucian culture. The Sabbat Lasombra should be recognizably distinct from the Lasombra antitribu in some fashion, and I don't think this was ever well presented.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with seeing many Lasombra of the time of the Anarch Revolt becoming hypocrites and power hungry, betraying their old ideals for power. I also don't have a problem for some opportunistic Lasombra who heed the old ways having joined the sect. Or that as time passed on the fires of youth faded, that some aspects of the old Lasombra culture came back. But there should also be a large number of Lasombra who continue to have the ideals of the original Lasombra anarchs who supposedly fought for freedom from the elders. And this last group of Lasombra has always been neglected in the game.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to figure out a way on how to combine the original ideals of the Anarch Revolt and the core Lasombra identity of them being ambitious and masters of intrigue, you could do a lot worse than the Path of Night.<br /> <br /> I think one issue is that the Path of Night was not one of the original Paths in the first Players Guide to Sabbat. So there obviously could not be any attempt to explain the clan using that Path. Instead, it was probably felt that all Sabbat Lasombra would adhere to a path like Power and the Inner Voice, Honorable Accord, or other more obvious leadership Path. I think the Path of Night first appears in the Revised VtM corebook where it's presented as a Path almost exclusively by very young Lasombra, who are scorned by the other Lasombra. (So your black sheep comment is on the mark).<br /> <br /> And like many concepts of the game, once its out there, it is often developed further by people who see potential in something, but don't adhere closely to details. So we can get to the point where we think the Path of Night is iconic to the Lasombra until it occurs to us this undermines other aspects of the clan like the OP mentioned. So if you want to say both aspects are true, it may be better to state that the Path of Night is something <i>distinctive</i> to the Lasombra (in the sense it reveals something unique about the clan), but isn't <i>iconic</i> (in the sense that it defines the clan).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are not completely right: what happened to the Lasombra was more like a coup d'etat. Gratiano killed his old master, and then approached the Friends of the Night and told them &quot;Join us&quot;. Friends thought about it, slid into the shadows and allowed the Clan as a whole to join the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> (and Sabbat culture has certainly influenced the Lasombra, exasperating their dark tendencies - from &quot;We Embrace whoever shows an attitude to power&quot; they went into full Darwinists, bent on destroying your life. Such a streak had always been there (see the Antediluvian with Montano and Gratiano), but it was hyped in the Sabbat, compared to their Dark Ages depiction in DA corebook and Libellus Sanguinis. They also went from &quot;We are Angels, and thus we can do whaetever we want&quot; attitude of the Cainite Heresy, or the &quot;we are agents of God's will&quot; ethos of the Road of Heaven, into more a &quot;We are the Scourge of God, the Tester of Sinners&quot; attituide of the new Path of Night.<br /> <br /> The fall of Tzimisce elders was more like the Bolsheviks, the Jacobines or the Maoists taking power (with the League of Oradea and Neo-Feudalists being the surviving elements of the Old Clan, a bit like surviving Orthodox priests in Soviet Union, the Directorate period in France or resurfacing Confucianism in China): Revised Clanbook stresses this by underlining how much the Clan has fallen into decadence, without the iron fist of the Elders reining in youngsters, metamorphosists and other oddities.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra are described more as &quot;Ok, old elites recognized the winning horse and joined&quot;, a la Nazi Germany or Fascist Italy: it's appropriate, in this context, that we have an ideologized minority of radical believers in Revolutionary Ideology, scoffing at the bourgeois habits of the upper echelons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-05-2022, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T12:49:32-08:00","id":1474051,"title":"","content":"Clan Trilogy Lasombra 3: Sacrifices, by Bruce Baugh, has a great narrative into what is to begin the path. Elieser de Polanco is the instructor and Lucita is the one being introduced to it. I'd recommend reading it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T15:21:04-08:00","id":1474522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5?p=1474051#post1474051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan Trilogy Lasombra 3: Sacrifices, by Bruce Baugh, has a great narrative into what is to begin the path. Elieser de Polanco is the instructor and Lucita is the one being introduced to it. I'd recommend reading it.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that trilogy really making me mad. I wonder what Anatole would have thought about Lucita seeking enlightenment by murdering orphans so she could be extra-bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T18:10:42-08:00","id":1474537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473917-help-me-understand-the-path-of-night-and-it-s-role-in-the-sabbat-pre-v5#post1473917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing thing has bugged me for almost 20 years. How the hell does a Path of Night adherent function within the Sabbat? It's lvl 2 sin is &quot;Accepting the superiority of another&quot;. How the hell does anyone except the Regent themselves not sin against this every single time they meet a Bishop, Arch Bishop, Cardinal etc.? I mean even having a Ductus would be a sin against this path.</div> </div> </div> </div>By making sure to think &quot;If only these inferior fools knew that I was totally just playing along with their orders as part of a long term plan and in reality don't acknowledge them as my superiors at all, MWAHAHAHAHA&quot; every time they run into a higher ranking person and have to take orders from them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T05:25:59-07:00","id":1524059,"title":"","content":"Well, that will go down to &quot;what's a superior&quot;. Lasombra in a most general way consider themselves to be the best, the apex of vampiredom. They may comply if someone prove to be a best planner or mystic or whatnot. But being better in a field is different of being intrinsically superior. So they will obey or disobey if that advance their agenda, but not because of the superiority of someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}